1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
And another fun thing we did in austin was visiting the state capital.
我们在奥斯汀做的另一件有趣的事，是参观州议会建筑；capital 为来源原词待核。

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:11,280
And if you've been on the channel for a while you know that I love history and official things and it's exactly what the free tours they offer are about.
看我频道久的人知道，我喜欢历史和官方事务，而这里提供的免费导览正好讲这些。

3
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:18,550
And the building itself is very beautiful and the tour is a fun intro to texas history which I know very little about.
建筑本身很漂亮，导览也有趣地介绍了得州历史，而我之前了解得很少。

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:23,600
And when you arrive in the hall you have this very beautiful floor with several coats of arms.
走进大厅，会看到很漂亮的地面，上面有好几个纹章。

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,000
And I was like I know this these are spain and france code of arms at the time.
我当时想：这些我认识，是那个时期西班牙和法国的纹章；code 原词待核。

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,760
And that's because texas has spanish and also french ties and keep that in mind because it's important for my next point.
那是因为得州与西班牙、法国都有渊源。记住这一点，后面我要讲的内容会用到。

7
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,519
Then we got to visit the house of representatives and senate chambers.
接着，我们参观了众议院和参议院议事厅。

8
00:00:37,519 --> 00:00:43,919
And this was pretty cool too because it gave me more insight on how a state government works today which to be honest I had no idea about.
这也很棒，让我更了解州政府如今怎样运作。说实话，我以前根本不了解。

9
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:48,799
And on our last texas trip we spent a bunch of time in the countryside because we were doing a road trip.
上次来得州，我们因为公路旅行，在乡村待了很多时间。

10
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:52,000
But I'd say the big event of this trip was the texas state fair.
但这次旅行的大活动，我会说是得州州博览会。

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,760
And I love the fair not only because I got to eat fried butter but also because it shows how much the country culture still influences city life today.
我喜欢这个博览会，不只是因为吃到了炸黄油，还因为它展示了乡村文化如今如何影响城市生活。

12
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:03,349
So the big thing we were excited for at the fair was the rodeo.
在博览会上，我们最期待的大事是牛仔竞技。

13
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:12,469
And I know on youtube you often have videos of europeans reacting to rodeos and you know they usually find that it's a big cultural difference and that they've never seen something like that.
我知道 YouTube 常有欧洲人看牛仔竞技的反应视频，通常会说文化差异很大，从没见过类似东西。

14
00:01:12,479 --> 00:01:18,239
But for me I had almost an opposite reaction because it reminded me of something I used to do as a kid.
但我的反应几乎相反，因为它让我想起小时候做过的事情。

15
00:01:18,239 --> 00:01:20,560
And I don't know it's maybe because of our shared history.
我也不确定，也许和我们共同的历史有关。

16
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:26,960
So as some of you know my dad is from the country of spain and he's from the region where the famous spanish bulls come from.
有些人知道，我父亲来自西班牙，而且来自那些著名西班牙公牛的产地。

17
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:34,150
And side note as a kid one of my biggest fears was to cross paths with one of these guys on my bike rides through the countryside.
顺便说，我小时候最怕的事之一，就是在乡下骑自行车时遇到这样一头牛。

18
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:37,519
Because they are pretty much everywhere in the fields in my region of spain.
因为在我家乡那个西班牙地区的田野里，它们几乎到处都是。

19
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:44,240
And the rodeo and cattle events really reminded me of something I used to experience every summer at my grandparents house in spain.
牛仔竞技和牛类活动，让我想起小时候每年夏天在西班牙祖父母家经历的事情。

20
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:52,720
Like growing up we had this event where like the whole village goes to an arena and then they let a young bull lose and you know the point is to try to run faster and avoid him.
小时候有种活动，全村人去竞技场，放出一头小公牛，大家要跑得快、避开它；lose 原词待核。

21
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:57,119
And obviously there's different sizes for different ages but everyone can participate.
当然，不同年龄对应不同大小的牛，但每个人都可以参加。

22
00:01:57,119 --> 00:02:01,176
So you know as a kid I was running with the bulls except that the bulls looked like this.
所以我小时候也“和牛一起跑过”，只不过牛长这样。

23
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:08,559
So yeah in texas I found that very cool that rodeo had kids events as well like calf scrambling or mutton busting.
所以我觉得得州牛仔竞技也有儿童项目很棒，比如 calf scrambling 或 mutton busting。

24
00:02:08,559 --> 00:02:15,999
And I love that in both places it's super familyfriendly like there are events that are fun for kids but there's also more serious ones for adults as well.
我喜欢两边都很适合全家参加：有儿童觉得有趣的项目，也有面向成年人的更严肃项目。

25
00:02:15,999 --> 00:02:23,360
All right now we're going to get into deeper topics so remember these are just my observations as a french person visiting texas.
好了，接下来会谈更深入的话题。记住，这些只是我作为法国游客来得州的观察。

26
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:29,119
So you're welcome to disagree and I even encourage you to share your thoughts about these topics in the comments.
欢迎不同意见，我甚至鼓励大家在评论里分享对这些话题的看法。

27
00:02:29,119 --> 00:02:33,680
But please please please do that respectfully and don't fight with others in the comments.
但请务必尊重地讨论，不要和评论区其他人吵架。

28
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:38,960
Because I already have enough people fighting about whether cornbread should be sweet or not in my barbecue video.
因为在我的烤肉视频里，已经有足够多人在争论玉米面包该不该是甜的了。

29
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:46,400
So one thing I noticed at the rodeo and that I found so interesting is how before the rodeo we all prayed for the contestants.
有件我在牛仔竞技现场注意到、觉得有趣的事，是比赛开始前我们一起为参赛者祈祷。

30
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:53,200
And again I have nothing against it because to be honest the contestants really need all the help they can get given what they are about to do.
我完全不反对，因为说实话，考虑到他们即将做的事，参赛者真需要一切能得到的帮助。

31
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:59,119
But in france you would never see religion at a public event because we don't have an official religion of the country.
但她说，在法国公共活动上不会看到宗教，因为法国没有国家官方宗教；这是作者的文化概括。

32
00:02:59,119 --> 00:03:04,640
And religion is seen more as a private thing you do on your own rather than something that belongs in the public space.
在她看来，宗教被更多看成私人做的事，而不是属于公共空间的东西。

33
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:10,960
So I don't know that's just a cultural observation that I found interesting because it was my first time ever praying at a public event.
所以，我不知道，这只是一个让我感兴趣的文化观察，因为这是我第一次在公共活动上祈祷。

34
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,320
That's not you know in a church or in a religious context.
不是在教堂里，也不是在宗教情境中。

35
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:17,840
So again here let me know your thoughts is that very common where you live.
所以，请告诉我你们的看法：你住的地方，这种情况常见吗？

36
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:21,520
But one thing I was surprised though to not see in public was politics.
不过，有个东西我没在公开场合看到，却让我意外：政治。

37
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:25,109
And here I know I'm getting on a dangerous topic so hear me out.
我知道这个话题可能敏感，先听我说完。

38
00:03:25,119 --> 00:03:31,510
You have to know that in france we have a strong culture of debate and we also like to disagree a lot with each other.
她说，在法国有很强的辩论文化，人们也喜欢彼此表达不同意见。

39
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:35,040
So people are going to volunteer their political thoughts very freely.
所以人们会很自然、很主动地说出政治看法。

40
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:40,800
Like I'm not even talking with friends but like when you're in a cab buying something or overall as part of small talk.
我说的甚至不只是朋友之间，而是坐出租车、买东西时，或者作为闲聊的一部分。

41
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:45,360
And I have to say that I'm not the biggest fan of this in france because I like to keep small talk light.
我并不是很喜欢法国这种情况，因为我喜欢让闲聊保持轻松。

42
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,480
And I prefer to focus on what I have in common with others.
我更喜欢关注自己与别人有什么共同之处。

43
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:53,439
And one stereotype that's often associated with texas is that it's a very conservative state.
人们常把得州与一种刻板印象联系起来，说它是个很保守的州。

44
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:57,760
And if you look at the stats texas definitely tends to lean a bit more conservative.
她说，如果看统计，得州确实倾向于更保守一点；此处是作者对统计的概括。

45
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,500
But I was surprised at how little people brought politics in a casual conversation.
但我很意外，在随意的交谈里，人们很少提政治。
